---
source: crates/dr-agent-tools/tests/catalog.rs
expression: table
---
asset.get [read] Read an asset's recorded metadata: kind, media type, size and pixel dimensions (the Stats tab's file readings).
book.get [read] Read book metadata and word targets; aggregate counts use the statistics adapter.
book.update [write] Update selected book metadata fields without replacing other book data.
book.writing_days [read] A book's writing days: words written per day (all devices), today, the last seven days, active days and the streak.
comment.anchors [read] The stored anchors of the comments on one entity's prose, for an editor laying them out (comments without an anchor are not listed).
comment.create [write] Add a comment or TODO, on an entity, a paragraph, a passage of its prose, a region of an image or PDF, or floating. Read the exact source prose before anchoring: a block needs that paragraph; ranges and anchor bytes need the full document. Entry anchors require an explicit prose module.
comment.list [read] List comments and TODOs (a target in the trash or gone shows as unlocated).
comment.reanchor [write] Put a comment's anchor back where the editor's undo brought its text back (the author's change, synced; it follows the editor's undo, so it is not an entry of the object-level undo). Read the comment and its complete source prose before setting an anchor; both versions are guarded. Clearing needs the comment read.
comment.update [write] Change a comment or TODO: its text, status (resolve / reopen), priority, kind or linked Agent conversation.
entry.create [write] Create an entry with its template, switch, residence, membership and initial module content.
entry.get [read] Read an entry including retained module values; an entry whose switch is on also carries what lies below it (resolved settings and their sources, children, members).
entry.list [read] Find entries, or list the entries living under one in manuscript order; with below, each listed entry whose switch is on carries its resolved settings, children and members.
entry.move [write] Move an entry's residence and manuscript position; the new residence is the root or a live entry whose switch is on.
entry.restore [write] Restore an entry and what lives under it from trash.
entry.set_level [write] Turn an entry's switch for what lives below it on or off. Turning it off moves its direct children (trashed ones included) to the root right after the top-level entry it lives under, each with its subtree, in one commit that one undo reverts; its settings, memberships and swimlane are kept and come back when it is turned on.
entry.trash [write] Trash an entry with what lives under it, keeping entries that only belong to it.
entry.update [write] Rename an entry, switch its template or change the overrides of what lives below it, without deleting retained content or touching its switch.
entry_history.restore [write] Restore selected entry metadata (switch included) or structural records from a snapshot as a new undoable commit.
entry_history.version [read] Read the current book version for per-entry snapshot restoration.
entry_relation_type.delete [write] Delete an unused unlocked relation type.
entry_relation_type.list [read] List relation types available to entry modules.
entry_relation_type.put [write] Create or edit a relation type with endpoint and template restrictions.
entry_template.delete [write] Delete an unused template without deleting its retained prose documents.
entry_template.list [read] List the templates of a book: modules, the switch's default, linkable, settings and actions.
entry_template.put [write] Create or replace a template definition (any modules, the switch's default, linkable, settings, actions) while retaining existing entry content and switches.
entry_template.put_module [write] Add or update a module definition of any kind on a template.
entry_template.remove_module [write] Remove a module definition while retaining values and prose on existing entries.
fact.list [read] List the book's project facts (项目设定), in order.
fact.put [write] Add a project fact or change one (key, value, position).
fact.remove [write] Remove a project fact.
history.points [read] List a prose document's history points (kept 30 days, at most one every 15 minutes of writing), newest first, with the words at each.
history.preview [read] Read a prose document as it was at a history point: its paragraphs (with H1/H2/H3 levels) and its owner's title and summary then.
material.create [write] Add a material: a text note, or an image or PDF whose asset is registered.
material.list [read] List materials in order, optionally of one folder.
material.move [write] Move a material in the list (only its own position changes).
material.update [write] Change a material's title, description, folder or TODO projection.
material_folder.create [write] Create a material folder.
material_folder.delete [write] Delete a material folder: its sub-folders and materials move up to its parent.
material_folder.list [read] List material folders (素材夹), parents before children.
material_folder.update [write] Rename or move a material folder.
membership.add [write] Add or order a membership without moving its residence.
membership.list [read] List valid memberships in a book.
membership.primary [write] Choose an existing membership as primary, or clear the primary membership.
membership.remove [write] Remove a membership and any timeline placements left without a lane. Requires a complete timeline_view.list at the guarded version; hidden timeline data prevents removal until the kernel cascade preserves it.
memory.add [write] Add a Project Memory entry (plain text; takes effect at once).
memory.list [read] List the book's Project Memory entries.
memory.remove [write] Remove a Project Memory entry (kept as removed; restorable).
memory.restore [write] Bring back a removed Project Memory entry.
memory.update [write] Change a Project Memory entry's text, kind or status.
module.list [read] List an entry's current and retained modules and their registered prose documents.
module.put_grid [write] Replace the rows, columns, cells and size of one plot module.
module.put_kv [write] Add or update an ordered key/value row in a module.
module.put_patch [write] Create or edit the text of a patch module record, preserving its source reference.
module.put_relation [write] Associate an entry with a live endpoint through its relations module.
module.read [read] Read a current or retained module and its structured content; a children module reads what lies below the entry.
module.read_prose [read] Read an entry's or a template's prose module with block IDs and version.
module.remove_kv [write] Remove a key/value row from a module.
module.remove_patch [write] Remove one patch record without deleting relations or other entries.
module.remove_relation [write] Remove one relation projected in an entry's relations module.
module.replace_prose [write] Replace an exact passage in an entry's prose module, addressed by block ID.
module.set_field [write] Set or clear a typed field value in an entry's fields module.
module.set_prose [write] Write paragraphs of an entry's or a template's prose module.
prose.link [write] Link anchored ranges of prose documents to entities (anchors, not positions: the undo of automatic links that were taken off).
prose.read [read] Read paragraphs of a prose document (text, block id, heading level).
prose.replace [write] Replace one exact passage of prose with new text (it must occur exactly once, in one paragraph).
prose.restore [write] Restore a prose document to an earlier version, as a new change (history stays).
prose.shape [read] Shape of a prose document: paragraphs, sentences, the share of dialogue, its checklist and the materials it embeds.
prose.unlink [write] Take links to entities off anchored ranges of prose documents (anchors, not positions: the undo of automatic links).
recent.list [read] List this device's live pages, retaining each entry's selected module.
relation.create [write] Create a canonical relation, validating live endpoints and template restrictions; return an existing semantic edge without a write.
relation.delete [write] Delete one canonical relation without deleting either endpoint.
relation.list [read] List canonical relations whose endpoints are live, optionally scoped to an endpoint or type.
timeline_view.delete [write] Delete a timeline view while retaining lane entries and memberships.
timeline_view.list [read] List timeline views with their effective lanes, placements and time pins.
timeline_view.place [write] Place or move an entry in a timeline, optionally joining a lane in the same commit.
timeline_view.put [write] Create or edit a timeline view, including its independent lane order. Whole-view replacement requires a complete timeline_view.list at the guarded version. Hidden lanes, placements or pin data prevent replacement; use supported item commands instead.
timeline_view.put_pin [write] Add or edit a time pin, optionally bound to any live entry.
timeline_view.remove [write] Remove an entry from a timeline lane and prune positions where it has no remaining lane. Requires a complete timeline_view.list at the guarded version; hidden timeline data prevents removal until the kernel cascade preserves it.
timeline_view.remove_pin [write] Remove a time pin from a timeline view.

